    "exit_rule": "drawer_position >= 0.29 at the final state (the demonstrated open stop is 0.30)",
    "guidance": "**Use:** Fresh-TCP local-increment prior requiring accurate drawer origin/orientation and desired opening (trained at 0.300 m). Its documented niche is a modest arm/path deviation in an otherwise training-like scene, including local correction from fresh measured TCP state. Such perturbed entries were not separately validated. In-distribution it passed 6/12 runs (50%), so treat it as a monitored secondary option rather than the nominal default.\n\n**Avoid:** Do not use it as recovery for large deviations, a missed handle/front, blocked drawer, distant/unreachable objects, or accumulated pose drift. Prefer H01 only when reliable cabinet displacement is the dominant consideration, and H03 for nominal geometry. Local increments are not globally object-displacement invariant.\n\n**Failure recognition:** Every validation run reached at least 0.29 m once (first crossing at steps 201–223; maximum 0.300 m), but six ended below the exit threshold at 0.13102–0.28257 m. Thus a transient opening is not completion. Watch for repeated local motion without drawer progress, subsequent drawer regression, unexpected drawer motion, growing TCP/front or TCP/red error, closure without red co-motion, red drop, IK nonconvergence, or limit contact; replan instead of allowing drift to accumulate.\n\n**Handoff:** For validated completion, verify `drawer_position >= 0.29` at termination. The 230:470 overlap permits transfer to `red_transfer` after opening above 0.26 m and red exposure; the cleaner cue is a stable drawer, released front, closed fingers, and observed red/TCP upward co-motion near the initial lift. The validation did not test the composed handoff."
  },
